Oh, but your first suggestion is spot on!  Well, maybe Bar can get by
w/o speed boots for a while, but we all want fixed speed boots in the
end.  Thinking about what would get this guy to the castle, where more
wishes await:

Do Sokoban before wishing for a bag of holding of amulet of
reflection.  If you survive (and you should) you will get one of
these.  In fact, I would suggest holding on to the wishes for a while.
 Head into the mines (with +2 DSM, you should have -1 AC with just
that) and pick up some random dwarven armor.  Making judicious use of
the altar in minetown, you should be able to get down to -6 - -8 AC
fairly easily.  The magic resistance from your DSM will prevent any
wand of deaths and polymorph traps, and the gnomes and dwarves will be
good cannon fodder for exercising your weapon skills of choice.

Once you finish the mines and sokoban, you'll have a better idea of
any equipment holes that you can fill with your remaining wishes.

Good luck, and play carefully!
